    "rationale": "We selected 1500 images per class from the Stanford Online Products training split (SOP_cls_train) to build a balanced primary training pool for chair, sofa, table, cabinet, and lamp. SOP_train is the most coherent multi-class source available among the allowed datasets for these classes, and it provides substantial per-class coverage (chair 5845, sofa 3472, table 5470, cabinet 5848, lamp 6304). The domain metadata shows domain 'products, fine_grained' with domain_alignment not marked as aligned, so we treat SOP as the best practical option for a unified, cross-class product-classification task given the constraints. Selecting only training data for the primary pool adheres to official-splits guidelines and avoids leakage from test splits. The target is 1500 images per class, totaling 7500 images for the primary pool. There was no explicit download budget constraint reported, so this configuration remains modest and suitable for CPU-based experimentation. If needed later, generalization data could be considered, but SOP provides a coherent, high-coverage starting pool for all five classes.",
